--- body ---
## Context

The author has reported for weeks that the sitter "tends to disappear on its
own from the installed-plugins list". Ticket 0688 investigated, ruled out both
mechanisms it had named (no Zotero update happened; the install used Tools ->
Add-ons -> Install Add-on From File, the persistent path), declined to invent
a third, and closed with the cause open and instrumentation added so the next
occurrence would leave evidence.

It occurred twice on the evening of 2026-09-06, during live verification, and
this time the evidence was collected while it was happening.

## What was observed

One Zotero session, started 20:56:31, never restarted:

- 23:0x  `verify` reports `present, version 0.2.13, active False, location app-profile`
- 23:35:59  `extensions/` and `extensions.json` both mtime-stamped; the record
  is gone and `extensions/sdt-pack-sitter@....xpi` is deleted from disk
- The running instance kept working from memory throughout -- the author could
  still open and close the dialog, and the toolbar spinner still animated.

So: registered, then DISABLED, then REMOVED, file and all, mid-session, with no
Zotero update and no user action. Disable-then-remove is what Gecko's
AddonManager does to an add-on whose update/compatibility check concludes there
is no compatible version of it.

## The mechanism this points at

`manifest.json` carries `applications.zotero.update_url`, and Zotero fetches it
on a timer after startup -- which is the one thing in this plugin that happens
minutes into a session, unprompted, matching the observed timing.

That URL resolves (HTTP 200) and returns a well-formed Mozilla update manifest
naming this add-on with an EMPTY updates array:

    "addons": { "sdt-pack-sitter@search-works-for-zotero.invalid": { "updates": [] } }

The reading to test is that Zotero takes "your id is listed, and it has no
versions" as "there is no compatible version of you", disables, and cleans up.

**This is why 0688's fix did not stop it.** 0688 changed `update_url` from
`https://example.invalid/...` (unreachable -> no version information) to a
reachable manifest carrying an empty list (-> still no version information).
Both hand Zotero the same answer. The change was a real fix to a real defect --
a URL chosen to never resolve -- and it did not touch this mechanism, which
nobody had identified. `update.json`'s own comment says as much and says it
honestly: "No claim is made either way about what an empty list or an
unreachable update_url does to an installed add-on -- that was not established
against Zotero's own fork."

## Relevant files

- `plugins/sdt-sitter/manifest.json` - carries `applications.zotero.update_url`
- `plugins/sdt-sitter/update.json` - the empty-updates manifest it names
- `bench/sdt_sitter_install.py` - `verify` reads the host's own record, and is
  what distinguishes the three states this defect passes through
- `tickets/closed/0688-sitter-persistent-install-and-manifest-id.erg` - the
  investigation this continues; read its log before adding a fourth guess

## Actions

1. Isolate, one variable. Build the current payload with `update_url` REMOVED
   and nothing else changed, install it, and leave Zotero running past the
   window in which the removal has been seen (~40 min). Zotero's own developer
   docs list only `applications.zotero` itself as required; 0688 read them and
   recorded that `update_url` "is nowhere stated as required". 0688 deliberately
   kept it rather than change two variables at once on a plugin already
   disappearing -- correct then, and the live reproduction is what now justifies
   testing the other arm.
   Probe build: 0.2.14, `update_url` removed, identical otherwise.
2. If it survives, that is the mechanism. Decide the permanent shape: drop
   `update_url` (no update channel exists, so it advertises nothing anyone can
   install), or publish a real entry per release with `update_link` and version
   bounds. Do not leave an empty list.
3. If it does NOT survive, the mechanism is elsewhere and this ticket has
   narrowed it by one: record that, and do not close the ticket with a guess.
   The next candidate to examine is the `.invalid` id under a host that may
   validate ids it never dereferences.
4. NEW, blocking 1-3 as filed: get a build installed at all, without GUI
   automation (2026-09-08's log entry -- xdotool cannot see this host's Zotero
   window, and a bare `extensions/<id>.xpi` drop does not register even after a
   full restart). Two candidates, neither tried yet:
   a. `--start-debugger-server` (listed in `zotero -h`) opens a devtools server
      that speaks Firefox's Remote Debugging Protocol, which -- unlike
      `--remote-debugging-port`'s CDP, which only reaches web content -- can
      attach to the chrome/browser process and eval privileged JS, including
      `AddonManager.installTemporaryAddon()` or a scripted disable/enable. No
      client for this protocol exists in this repository; building one is real
      work, not a one-line probe.
   b. Ask the author to do one GUI install via Tools -> Add-ons -> Install
      Add-on From File (the path that worked for fulltext-control), then drive
      only the disable/enable/replace steps by hand at his direction while this
      session watches `sitter-watch.log`. Cheaper, but needs him at the
      keyboard for each cycle rather than an unattended run.

## Test

`scratchpad/sitter-watch.sh` polls the three facts 0688's three-state model
separates -- record present, record active, XPI on disk -- plus Zotero's pid,
and appends a line ONLY on a change. A quiet log is "nothing moved"; a line is
the transition, stamped. It was started at 23:42 and is what should carry the
verdict for action 1 rather than anyone's recollection of when the icon went.

## Verification

- [ ] The probe build (no `update_url`) survives a Zotero session longer than
      any build carrying one has
- [ ] `sitter-watch.log` shows the survival as an absence of transitions, over
      a window that previously contained one
- [ ] A build WITH `update_url` restored disappears again -- the control that
      makes the survival mean something rather than a quiet evening

## Invariants

- Do not "fix" this by having the installer reinstall the plugin on a timer.
  That hides a host decision the plugin should not be arguing with, and would
  make the next occurrence invisible again.
- `bench/check_sitter_version.py`'s guard stands: any payload change needs its
  own version number, probe builds included.

## Exit criteria

The disappearance has a named, demonstrated mechanism and a fix whose control
arm has been run in both directions -- or, if `update_url` is exonerated, this
ticket records that with its evidence and hands on the next candidate.
